# L §5.10 Kind and unit: "unit(x) of a one-unit place, and unit(q) of a quantity, a leg's amount included, are the unit
# as a key of the unit kind that holds it (currencies for a currency, §5.7)"; "Where load can't see the key (a leg
# declared with a unit kind), it is read per value". buy's cash leg is in PLN, its units leg in fund_x, a key of notes;
# konto is a PLN place. (Writer 8, sixth pass: refcore read unit(x) of a place only, found with C3-13's example arc.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2024-12-31
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2024-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind notes: unit
kind brokerages: place any min 0
kind trades: event certain
  leg units: notes
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input n_units: num
input amt: money PLN
input day: date

move buy: trades
  on day
  leg units from market to mbank amount n_units * 1 fund_x
  leg cash from konto to market amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2024-01-01
  notes + [fund_x] lives 2000-01-01..
  brokerages + [mbank] lives 2010-01-01..
  n_units = 10
  amt = 1 000.00 PLN
  day = 2024-03-01
  opening[konto] = 5 000.00 PLN at 2024-01-01 start

ask q: unit(buy.cash.amount), unit(buy.units.amount), unit(buy.units.amount) == fund_x, unit(konto)
=== expect
q: (PLN, fund_x, true, PLN)
  cut 2024-12-31
